---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="Franchise Loan Stats sets no cookies, shows no ad trackers and collects no personal details. This page lists exactly what is measured and who processes it." crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">No cookies, no accounts, no advertising trackers.</p>
    <h2>What is measured</h2>
    <p>The site counts page views and a few actions (using search, a filter, the compare tool, the calculator, a download, or a click on an outbound link) with PostHog, hosted in the European Union. It runs in a cookieless mode: nothing is stored on your device, visits are not linked across sessions, IP addresses are anonymised by the analytics project's settings, and session recording is off. If your browser sends "Do Not Track", nothing is recorded.</p>
    <p>Numbers you type into the calculator stay in your browser and are not sent anywhere.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>Pages are served by GitHub Pages, which processes visitor IP addresses in its server logs under GitHub's own privacy terms.</p>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>If you write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>, your message and address are kept only to reply and keep a record of corrections. The mailbox is hosted by AgentMail and may be read and answered with the help of AI software acting for the site owner.</p>
    <h2>Partner links</h2>
    <p>If a page carries a labelled partner link and you click it, the destination site applies its own privacy policy and may record that you arrived from here.</p>
    <h2>Data about businesses and borrowers</h2>
    <p>The SBA's public file names individual borrowers. This site does not publish borrower names, addresses or single-loan records, only aggregate statistics.</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>This page is updated when practices change. The site's source history shows every revision.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
